{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1496039-question-about-scale","id":1496039,"title":"Question about Scale","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-01T08:04:46-07:00","id":1496039,"title":"Question about Scale","content":"Quantum 10 would allow Quantum anima 10. Does this mean the nova could move say a star or planet? If so any idea what a difficulty like that would be ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T08:23:00-07:00","id":1496042,"title":"","content":"Unless you're Divis Mal, hitting Quantum 10 causes you to ascend beyond the known universe. OTOH it is possible to Max Out Quantum Anima 9 to achieve an effective level of 10. You may still be unable to lift a star/planet because you would presumably have to split your effort between the size and the weight of the object moved. After all, there are differences between lifting something the size of a cruise ship and something the weight of a cruise ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T14:29:15-07:00","id":1496066,"title":"","content":"it seems the novas of version 2 are considerably underpowered compared to version 1. Why would he need to spit effort Quantum 9 with a nine in anima would allow the movement of a star or planet. just looking at the scale table. is there more to read on the scale table and how to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T15:10:14-07:00","id":1496069,"title":"","content":"Actually, a planet is Scale 8 and a star would be scale 9, so you dont really need Q10 to move a star, so Q8 Nova would be capable of moving earth, and Q9 an star (and virtually an entire star system).<br /> <br /> It is not a big deal, the scale is sponential, we are scale 1, a truck is 2, a 747 is 3, a Destroyer ship is 4, the largest structures we ever created is 5, 6 is a entire city or a montain, 7 is a entire continent, 8 is an entire planet and 9 is a star / star system (Sun is like 98% of the entire system weight).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T18:30:43-07:00","id":1496079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logansrun68</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1496039-question-about-scale?p=1496066#post1496066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems the novas of version 2 are considerably underpowered compared to version 1. Why would he need to spit effort Quantum 9 with a nine in anima would allow the movement of a star or planet. just looking at the scale table. is there more to read on the scale table and how to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd split the effort to prevent starting characters (or their nemesis) from picking up and throwing Manhattan Island (or the planet Earth) whenever they want.<br /> <br /> Starting novas get 150 xp. Buying Quantum up to 4 costs 48 xp. Mega-Might 1 costs 12 xp. Mega-Lifting costs 12 xp. Mega-Might 1 gives you Scale 2 for lifting and moving, and lets you throw anything you lift. Mega-Lifting lets you spend Quantum Points equal to your Quantum rating to boost your lifting capacity by the number of Quantum Points spent, so by spending 4 Quantum Points you temporarily boost your lifting capacity to Scale 6. Using your assumption, he can pick up and throw Manhattan as a character who has used less than 1/3 of his starting xp. That is obviously not how the rules are intended to work.<br /> <br /> Since you've still got 68 unspent xp, you may as well buy Mega-Might up to 4 for an additional 36 xp. Mega-Might 4 gives you Scale 5 for lifting and moving, and lets you throw anything you lift. Mega-Lifting lets you spend Quantum Points equal to your Quantum rating to boost your lifting capacity by the number of Quantum Points spent, so by spending 4 Quantum Points you temporarily boost your lifting capacity to Scale 9. Using your assumption, he can pick up and throw Earth as a character who has used about 4/5 of his starting xp. That is obviously not how the rules are intended to work.<br /> <br /> Look at the Scale examples on page 164 of Aberrant. Might 3 is a gorilla. Size 3 is a small building. Can gorillas pick up small buildings? Not unless they're King Kong. Gorillas (and most novas) are size scale 1, so they suffer from a Scale difference when lifting large objects. Now if a nova wanted to pick up a scale 1 object that happened to weigh as much as a building, that'd be a different matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 11-01-2022, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T19:19:38-07:00","id":1496080,"title":"","content":"The problem there is not really splitting effort, but how Mega Lift and Mega Crush work (and it becomes really bizarre really fast). I would say even letting Mega Attributes as one scale above the other powers is something I would avoid (I have a few suggestions in my book, but its not the point here).<br /> <br /> We are not talking about these two, as logansrun68 specifically asked about Quantum Anima. The scales table are broken as a general rule, but size is the most solid of them, as there is a clear measurable grow of mass, starting somewhere at human size and growing pretty fast.<br /> <br /> Different from other games that have a small difference between different sizes, to the point a big person is considered a different size, Storypath scale is all about huge differences. The idea of scale is something normal people just cant beat unless specifically trained for that, for example, a very capable power lifter can lift an scale 2 object, and the Olympic sprinters can run at scale 2. Our characters are not normal people, even Talents can do impossible things, that\u2019s why they can consider the scale gap as a significant increase in difficulty instead of impossible.<br /> <br /> Now for difficulties, things in the same scale have difficulties between 0 (really easy, would not matter to roll if not for complications and possible stunts) and 5 (next to impossible, virtually in the margin of next scale).<br /> <br /> So lets say you are trying to lift something your size scale, the difficulty will be 0 to something light to 5 for something really heavy, but its not only a matter of weight, it matter how easy or hard it is to grab and how easy or hard it is to balance the thing you are trying to lift. An object one size smaller should be so easy to lift it doesn\u2019t need a roll, and an object one size larger should be just impossible to lift.<br /> <br /> Now a Talent or Nova with no Mega Might try to do the same, to them lifting a rock the size of a person (difficulty 5) would be as hard as lifting a big cow (difficulty 3 +2 from their size scale 2).<br /> <br /> And then we go for the next level, a Nova with Might Scale N (for any number you pick from 1 to 10), When they try to lift an object size N they need to roll, the same way as a person need to roll for lifting objects size 1, but if the object is size N-1 it worth no effort, so no need to roll.<br /> <br /> Back to Quantum Anima, moving a object the size of the character can lift with the power will require some test, so moving the Sun with Quantum Anima 9 will require a lot of effort, because the sun is pretty big, but moving a really big star (many times the size of the sun) will be more difficult (increase difficulty, not scale). If the Nova can increase their scale to 10 using Maxing out, they can move the sun or virtually any star with little to no effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T14:26:54-07:00","id":1496127,"title":"","content":"It may be a bit too hand-wavy, and I may be remembering 1e rules, but I believe that Mega-Might/Mega-Lifting etc. do allow the nova to lift larger size objects as well. The explanation is that their Quantum essentially holds the object together while they lift it (assuming it is not structurally made that way). That way, you do get the thematic nova throwing a tank, or catching a crashing aircraft for example. Essentially, the assumption was that if the nova had the strength, then they had the leverage, could probably get a grip on it, and it would hold together through their quantum (at least until it landed on something they may have thrown it at).<br /> <br /> This holds true, but even more so for Quantum Anima, where it is even easier to argue that the Quantum is keeping it together, there is no leverage, or grip issue to speak of. So the only remaining issue is Might.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T15:06:47-07:00","id":1496129,"title":"","content":"Sure you can keep everything intact (or almost) by using Mega Might, no need of any kind of leverage or proper grapping position.<br /> <br /> Mega Lift allow you to add many scales (up to quantum) to your carrying capacity, RAW it means a Quantum 2 with Mega Might 2 can lift a Aircraft carrier.<br /> <br /> It sounds hand wave but it actually is how I use it, there is no RAW description of how lifting things work or anything similar. Feel free to ignore my suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T19:09:09-07:00","id":1518595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1496039-question-about-scale?p=1496042#post1496042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're Divis Mal, hitting Quantum 10 causes you to ascend beyond the known universe. OTOH it is possible to Max Out Quantum Anima 9 to achieve an effective level of 10. You may still be unable to lift a star/planet because you would presumably have to split your effort between the size and the weight of the object moved. After all, there are differences between lifting something the size of a cruise ship and something the weight of a cruise ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading Quantum Anima and over all it does not mention needing to split between mass and size. It seemed more that you would choose the files you are choosing to manipulate. So if your lifting a target often you would use mass as that is the man arena you would work with even to the power calling towards it and if you w acted to say move a large cloud or a bank of fog, toxic gas or just dust you might shift into the size arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}